  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Phenol has activating (electron releasing) $-\\mathrm{OH}$ group and bromine water supplies $\\mathrm{Br}^{+}$ ion easily, hence under such conditions reaction does not stop at monobromo or dibromo stage but a fully brominated $(2,4,6$,-tribromophenol) compound is the final product.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/PMaewaCy9T_9wFUxR2-Q64c5ir_XzXOhczzh8eQsOoo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
